  "start": 2356.18,
  "end": 2412.3799999999997,
  "text": "I don't know if the Council is aware, I think maybe some of you might individually have been made aware, but I wanted to make it public record that Oxhill has now been sued a second time about two weeks ago in federal court for non-payment to the current architect Thomas Juhal Hansen of the city center West condos part of their development. So I think the city council needs to look really closely when they're thinking about working with these types of development companies to see if they're actually solvent because these guys have three lawsuits now for non-payment. They don't look to be terribly solvent. My last comment is about the budget proposal that we witnessed at that particular meeting from your city planner. The rate of increase in all of the taxes overall was really significant, right? A 20-something percent, I think, overall from last year's budget, which that seems like"
