  "text": "But the property taxes in particular are outrageous and just three days after the meeting, we all got our bills and to give you an example for me personally, like the year before last my bill increased by $250. And then last year it increased by $600. Well this year under that new proposal with his new property tax with no cuts, it's a $2400 increase. With runaway inflation, I don't think most people can afford that kind of an increase to their monthly mortgage every month."
