  "start": 4479.58,
  "end": 4577.02,
  "text": "would be six feet in every world spot. Okay and how wide is the shared use path that's going? 10 feet. Okay so I will again strongly request that those two be combined I think if and if that's not going to happen for some reason I feel like I could get some consensus on that. I would also then like to offer consideration for moving the shared use path onto the chambered road side of the berm. I recognize it might not be able to be 10 feet wide. That's okay. I think that if kids can be expected to walk along a five to six foot sidewalk a bike that's passing along there would be just fine. I also would like to point out that the other side of chambered road that backs up to where the assembly is. That's currently sidewalk maybe there's a plan to make that a 10 foot shared use path. I think that's a bit excessive but I also think that in recognition of what our neighborhood is losing and the amount of public disdain for this project that there are still there's still an opportunity for the neighborhood to be overall be made happy and let me just be very clear I'm not speaking for everyone in my neighborhood I understand that I recognize that I'm not speaking for everyone that drives through my neighborhood. I'm speaking for the large number of people that turned out in the past two years or three years that we've been doing this process. So let me be clear and not everyone but there are still opportunities to make this compatible."
