  "speaker_source_detail": "diarize library (15 speakers) + local Whisper transcription",
  "start": 4854.3,
  "end": 4907.98,
  "text": "And I don't have the numbers in front of me but in previous presentations we've shared information regarding conflict points when we talk a lot about conflict points and we can recirculate that but we can't necessarily predict a comparable accident or crash number in a future year but what we can evaluate and understand is what are the number of conflict points points where vehicles potentially applied or vehicles pedestrians bikes whatever it may be. We know how many of those there are today and we also know that in the reconfigured condition there would be a certain number as well. Again I don't have the numbers in front of me and we can go back and pull those and circulate that but there was a substantial reduction in this reconfigured condition in the number of conflict points which generally would suggest that you are we are addressing the safety issues that are leading to those crashes."
