  "text": "signal. Councillor Piederson. Two things first with respect to council number halls comments from requests as a general matter it does seem to me that separating sidewalks and bike acts like paths should be a last resort and not a first resort it seems redundant in a lot of cases and the ten foot wide configuration is widely used precisely for this purpose even new paths that are being constructed for instance in the county and I do have to wonder whether that is a smarter way to go here and support of that suggestion. The second question I have is I'm trying to do my best to follow maps I'm going to need a little bit of help here but if you look at where chambered road and eaten place intersect and you head down eaten place to willow with it, etc that area we see a shared use path that cuts across eaten place but it doesn't turn down eaten place even though we have an existing sidewalk there and that transitions rather quickly into a seven foot sidewalk and ultimately a ten foot when you get farther on perfects bulldozer but there doesn't seem to be a connection anticipated here with bike and pedestrian use on eaten place and I may be misreading the map but I am curious to know because it would seem to me that we should be supporting bike and in for bike and pedestrian infrastructure development on eaten place and this would be the time"
