  "text": "Hello. I'm Karen Grace, which three five away Winston plays in Cobdale. And I say, thank you very much for asking about the sidewalk width. Because that's one thing I was very concerned about with all the students and parents walking from assembly to the new school bus stop, you need more than the basic sidewalk really. And also, that sidewalk could provide access for people like myself to get over to the bus stops on 123. So don't think that it's just for school to talk. Please. And I'm hoping that the new sidewalk, oh, Department Avenue that is being planned will be wide enough for two people with walkers to pass without running out of the grass or into the street. Which means more than five foot, please. It's got to be the width of two. Two of these with a little room for elbows. Now, so please, six foot at least. And that's not including the curb that this is not safe to be running on a curb. I walk with you. I walk too much and I'm sure most people with walkers do. The other thing, I like the idea of combining the shared use path with the sidewalk that sounds like a practical way to get the extra width you need for the various purposes. And actually simplify things. And for each and place, everywhere you can go to a wider sidewalk now, rather than having to say, oh dear, we should have made it wider to match what's further along. Do it now when it's, you know, when you don't have to tear out what you've already paid for to put in something wider. I think that's that's pretty much all. I may have a few minor things to comment online. But those are the major points I want to make. Thank you."
