  "start": 6776.94,
  "end": 6834.86,
  "text": "teachers and administrators custodial food service and support staff, purchase and maintain buses, hire and train drivers, secure licensing, insurance and operational systems. We would lose access to some educational offerings and infrastructure we currently benefit from, as we do not have the student capacity to support all programming such as leveled AAP programming. Certain special education services access to 40 AP courses than the IB program, language immersion programs, elementary foreign language, some middle school high school elected courses, eight high school world languages, eight academy programs, competitive athletics, and a wide range of extra curricular offerings. If this option is to be considered, I respectfully request a council fund an independent consultant to assess the full financial and educational impact this will have on our students and our taxpayers. Thank you. Our next speaker is Jennifer DeSonna."
