  "start": 6996.86,
  "end": 7049.18,
  "text": "The program leverages the same participation that we're ensuring consistent activity that reinforces Fairfax's literary presence throughout the year. Currently, the park and wrecked department has been directed by the city council to perform a 10% reduction exercise as part of fiscal planning. Their preliminary proposal estimates eliminates the $25,000 allocation for fall for the book, along with funding for the city of Fairfax, the Air Company and Fairfax Band. There's a Belvin Redline in this proposed 10% exercise. This is not a final decision. It's a step towards understanding the council's ability to make adjustments to the budget. I look forward to speaking with you more on this at the next two public meetings. Thank you very much. Our next speaker is Marianna Fornier."
