  "start": 7266.62,
  "end": 7369.42,
  "text": "Good evening. I'm Paul Hopkins. I live at 10773 Crest Street. I'm going to talk about property tax for a minute. My wife and I have lived in Verifact City for 19 years. I really enjoy it here. We recently received a 25-25 real estate property notice assessment change. The proposed tax increase is estimated to be 20.1% higher than it was last year. Typically it's been running 3 to 5% each year. This was a shock to us. When we looked at it closer and talked to some of the neighbors, it turns out that half of the increase is due to a 10% plus up in the cost property values. That's common throughout the whole neighborhood. The other half is due to the increased real estate tax rates that are being proposed. We're retired and we're on a fixed income. For us to come up with more money, it means we have to reduce some place else, obviously. We'll have to increase goes as proposed, then we'll have to come up with money from other parts of our current budget. Because like I said, our income is fixed. I don't have any other sources of bringing income in. I'm asking the honorable mayor and city council members to take consideration those of us who are on fixed incomes and retired as you decide the new fiscal fiscal year, 26 budget. Thank you."
