  "text": "schools having English there for a long time. I don't envy you, your decisions you need to make, and the trade-offs you need to make. I want to thank the staff for the preparation of the budget. I also want to particularly call out Christine Johnson, who is answered by incessant emails a whole host of times to help me understand what's going on with the taxes assessment. I want to take two comments, make two comments, and one recommendation. First comment is around community interest, second comment is around my self-interest, and then I'll get to the recommendation. When it comes to community interest, I have to say that I believe we face a really difficult financial situation coming up, because of the cutbacks in the federal government, it's estimated that for every federal employee that's laid off of fire, there's two to three contractors who are laid off in fire. Now, you know the demographics of the city better than I do. And so the impact of those cutbacks are going to hit the people who are paying the taxes here. I'm gratified to hear that that you're going to be talking to Fairfax County public schools about the assessment, and what that and the levy on our school system, obviously I'm interested in that because of my wife's contribution at Fairfax City High School. But I think we really have to look carefully at this budget given our future financial situation. My self-interest, my wife is already on a fixed-end come. I am quickly moving to a fixed-end come. The rate of increase in the the 9 to 10 percent in the tax rate is going to be really tough to swallow as we looked to our future. Similar to the gentleman who just spoke, we've lived here for 15 years, we've made friends, neighbors, taken advantage of the cultural opportunities that have been talked about here. We love this community, we don't want to have to make a decision to have to leave. But with this kind of increase, this is going to be tough. To my recommendation, my recommendation is to slow down. It's to slow down on the rate of increase, push back on Fairfax County public schools as much as possible. Perhaps look at a four to five percent increase in the tax rate for the for the tax assessment. Again, thank you for your time. Thank you for your service. Good luck with this. Is there anybody else in the"
