  "text": "Good evening, council. Thank you for the opportunity to speak. My name is Derek Scott. I am the current director of the City of Fairfax Band Association. And I sent a virtual comment earlier, but I felt in solidarity with our colleagues in the Fairfax theater company and the fall for the books. I would read my comment publicly. The City of Fairfax Band has its formation right here. 1969. We performed our first concert outside of City Hall. Because of the city support organization is celebrating its 50-50 year, which is a remarkable milestone for any organization. The City of Fairfax Band Association started here. This concert was first of many that not only sought to create music of the highest quality from our residents of the city and county, but also to show the world that the City of Fairfax has one of the best and most celebrated community bands in the country. Our organization performs over 50 events per year, including the 4th of July parade, numerous summer events, official installation ceremonies, funerals, and many other city sponsored events as requested. Like the most recognizable events the City Council to the council is our summer programming and our onerflight ensemble. The onerflight ensemble, which started in 2010, is easily one of the most moving groups in the City of Fairfax Band Association. This group led by City resident Jeff Saffins. Welcome to veterans to Dolas Airport and Reagan National as they come to visit their monuments for the time."
